From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:00:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui, acp_thread: message times and turn duration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.4 (ask 24). Each user message shows when it was
sent, right-aligned under it; each completed turn's last agent message
shows when it ended and how long the turn took ("09:16 · 1m 30s"). The
full date is in a tooltip. Shown regardless of `show_turn_stats`.

acp_thread keeps the times in a side table, `message_times`, one slot per
entry, kept in step by push_entry and truncate_entries, so rewind drops
them. A side table rather than a field on UserMessage/AssistantMessage:
those literals span upstream's native agent (agent/thread.rs, db.rs),
26 sites a bump would have to carry. A chunk's time is the agent's
`_meta.claudeCode.timestamp` (Claude Agent (Plus) >= 0.37.0 stamps every
chunk, live and on replay), on the v1 and the keyed v2 path, else the
receive time, but only while a turn runs: a replayed chunk received now
says nothing about when it was sent, so an agent without the field shows
times live only. The local prompt is stamped when it is sent.
turn_duration runs from the user message to the turn's last agent
message, and is None while that turn still runs.

The row is added once, where render_entries wraps each entry, so
render_entry is untouched.

Tests, each seen failing first: acp_thread_message_times_tests.rs (agent
meta on replay, no time without one, a live turn's receive time, rewind)
and thread_view/tests/message_time_tests.rs (the rows and the duration;
nothing without a time).
---

